  "initial_review": "Four non-exclusion chunks after two blank-only restorations: registry facade include, CPU40 memory-sizing rationale, platform branch rewrite and added endif. Fifteen pure exclusions.",
  "counter_review": "RegOpenKeyEx/RegQueryValueEx/RegCloseKey need overlay routing, but the common/wow/registry.h included transitively already supplies every used mapping. Direct narrower include removes product-internal dependency without changing target functions. Original non-i386 formula retains DPMI headroom before SAS allocation, necessary for selected software machine; the extra _M_IX86 && !CPU_40_STYLE conditional can be reduced after actual supported profile checks while preserving original i386 frame and selected calculation.",
  "evidence": "config.c read_profile_int and GetVDMSize Reg* calls; common/wow/registry.h maps all used APIs. mvdm_shadow_registry.h adds unused Nt* aliases and lifecycle declarations. config.c selected GetVDMSize/max(XMS+EMS+1024+DPMI) feeds sas_init; original formula already exists in non-i386 branch.",
  "limits": "Only blank formatting changed; functional recommendations not implemented."
